module gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, quote, li, ul }

// This intention consumes the operator's declared-relationship ruling. It does not choose a
// transparent-reference spelling: the existing equals form's behavior is an observation, not that
// decision. The relationship, its surface, and the compiler's enforcement are separate obligations.

fn derived_types_keep_their_name_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`): it holds what, why and done-when, never the how. Work items, their order and their staffing are selected against this intention and live under the roadmap in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority`; a work item names this intention, the intention does not list its work items."),
      p(text: "**Grounding (rulings cited, not minted):** `gunbc.design_ruling::declared_intent_separates_independent_choices_2026_11_23` and `gunbc.design_ruling::type_relationships_are_declared_and_transparent_reference_is_explicit_2026_11_23` govern the declared relationship; `gunbc.design_argument::declared_intent` supplies the general argument. The sibling `gunbc.design_ruling::value_disposition_and_named_binding_use_are_explicit_2026_11_23` applies the same distinction to value disposition, not a spelling for type relationships. The existing `gunbc.design_ruling::where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors`, `gunbc.design_ruling::nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved`, `gunbc.design_ruling::machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier` and `gunbc.design_ruling::literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim` keep their scopes. `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority`, `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization`, `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration` and `gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate` govern authority, the shared judgment, migration and conversions."),
      p(text: "**Honest scope:** a transparent reference is admitted when the author has explicitly selected that relationship; it denotes the same full type and adds no constraint or nominal guarantee. A refinement, brand or nominal distinction is not erased because its representation matches the base. The existing `type A = B` spelling is NOT hereby selected as transparent-reference syntax. The operator reads `a = b` as suggesting a value copy and wants a reference to be clear and analogous to other reference features; that is a surface-design question, not a ruling about runtime physical copying. Its spelling and meaning must be recorded before a reference-specific semantic cut relies on them; independently ruled constraint and nominal enforcement does not wait on that spelling. No blanket alias deletion, blanket refusal of `MyStr = String`, or generic-versus-nongeneric exemption is inferred here."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "Intention (what)"),
    p(text: "**What:** the relationship the author declares between types survives resolution, inhabitance and realization. A transparent reference denotes the same full type expression; additional constraints remain obligations; a nominal distinction remains distinct; and an independently governed definition does not inherit equality or guarantees merely from its origin. ONE root inhabitance judgment with the resolved declarations decides the relationship and any declared conversion in its actual direction. A common representation or expanded head is not enough to decide it. The language must distinguish these intentions without requiring another relationship taxonomy or mechanism before a concrete consumer needs it."),
    p(text: "A reference to `Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<8>>` denotes that FULL constrained composition. It neither introduces an independent numeric model nor erases the width. The intersection ruling remains authoritative; the existing phantom implementation is a reported enforcement gap, not an exception that claims no guarantee. Whether a type expression has parameters does not decide whether its name is transparent, constrained or nominal."),
    p(text: "**Why:** the operator's 2026-11-19 alias question exposed accepted values whose expected constraint or nominal distinction was not enforced. The 2026-11-23 clarification separates that defect from an intentionally transparent reference: either relationship is acceptable when its intention is clear, and additional names and mechanisms should be minimized for now. The intended guarantee is preservation of the declared relationship, not refusal whenever two spellings differ."),
    h2(text: "Evidence and its limits"),
    p(text: "The recorded `probe.alias_interchange` suite ran the v1 seed CompileAccept path through `gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census` in one `gunbc run --claim-run` process; its receipt is in `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::an_int_argument_inhabits_a_nat_parameter_at_typecheck`. It admitted a String-typed VARIABLE at `std.types` `NonEmptyStr`, branded `PathSegment`, local `type MyStr = String`, and local `type MySecret nominal_opaque = String`, each with zero blocking rows. The general argument check did refuse Int-at-record, String-at-record and Int-at-String, while base-at-base and derived-at-derived stayed clean. These are source observations on v1, not executed evidence about v2. The real-path v2 verdict over the actual standard-library declarations remains owed; two-declaration stand-ins and a required gate's overall status do not establish it."),
    p(text: "The recorded source analysis locates alias/refinement transparency in `v1.compiler.infer::declared_type_inhabitance`, `v1.compiler.infer_types::alias_identity_in_judgment` and the nonblocking `UndecidableRefinementIntroduction` result. That explains why common representation is a candidate cause, not why every accepted same-base pair is wrong. In particular, acceptance of `MyStr = String` is not a negative control until that declaration's relationship is decided. Once expressed with the selected transparent-reference surface, same-identity acceptance belongs among the positive controls. Constraint or nominal erasure remains a separate negative control."),
    h2(text: "Done-when"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "The transparent-reference surface and its same-identity meaning are chosen and recorded under the type-relationship ruling before their use in a reference-specific semantic change or migration. It is visibly distinguished from introducing a value binding, a restriction or a nominal boundary. Existing equals-form acceptance is an observation, not the authority for that choice; no physical-copy behavior is inferred from a reader's expectation. This pending choice does not block probes or repairs whose constraint or nominal contract is already settled."),
      li(text: "The real in-scope v2 acceptance path preserves each declared relationship through one root judgment. Transparent same-identity references, whether generic or nongeneric, remain accepted; a base value without the required construction or evidence cannot enter a constrained or nominal position merely because both realize to the same representation. Each direction of a crossing follows its declared conversion authority. Base-at-base and correctly constructed values stay accepted. Receipts name the exact path exercised; any justified seed mirror is reported separately under the v1 purpose test."),
      li(text: "The ruled where-refinement surface retires to checked constructors returning Optional, with carried evidence only where its named authority permits it. NonEmptyStr and the migrated brands retain their actual contracts; a rejected construction is never promoted to a value. The literal-only interim scaffold is retired when its declared replacement capability is established, not merely because this plan exists."),
      li(text: "A transparent reference to the width composition preserves the full intersection and the width's identity. The accepted control is a correctly admitted width value; the negative control is an out-of-range or unproved base value crossing that boundary. The intersection is not flattened into its base, and parameterization supplies no exemption from this rule."),
      li(text: "Changing or removing a source form does not silently reinterpret its consumers. A bounded migration names the affected declared relationships and preserves their obligations; remaining implementation gaps name their trigger. There is no completion claim based only on deleting aliases, counting rewritten files or making the original four observations all refuse."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "Realization (downstream)"),
    p(text: "The existing work-item identities and their dependency graph remain in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority`, bound here through `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_intention_binding`. A small reference-specific slice settles its surface on distinguishing examples before changing that relationship's semantics or migrating references. Independently, real v2 probes and shared-judgment repairs for already settled constraint and nominal contracts can proceed, as can the bounded work realizing the existing where-retirement ruling. The unresolved reference spelling is not a new gate on that work. Full node acceptance still requires all its controls and existing dependencies; an independent repair does not establish completion of the relationship program. Seed changes remain subject to `gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing`; a v1 observation never supplies a missing v2 receipt. The work is judged by the relationships and contracts its executing paths preserve, not by the number of renamed declarations."),
  ]
}

data derived_types_keep_their_name_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "derived-types-keep-their-name",
  title: "Declared type relationships survive: explicit transparent references, preserved constraints and nominal distinctions, and checked construction",
  body: derived_types_keep_their_name_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "The declared-relationship done-when holds by execution: the transparent-reference surface is recorded, same-identity references remain admitted, constraints and nominal distinctions survive the shared judgment and in-scope realization, width references retain the full constrained intersection, and the ruled where surface retires to checked construction without silent reinterpretation of consumers. The real v2 path is evidenced separately from seed observations.") },
}
